{"step_index":692,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:56:12Z","input_tokens":2801,"cache_read_tokens":176088,"output_tokens":2604,"thinking":"The code uses compat syntax within `teacher.html`, dictated by the use of compat Firebase libraries. The function retrieves submissions for a quiz, ordering them by submission time in descending order. Upon snapshot updates, it fetches all submission documents, then updates a count badge.\n\n\nDisplays the student submission cards with key information including name, section, score, violations, time taken, timestamp, and an expandable summary. An error check is included: if Firestore rules block submission reading, a helpful alert guides the user to update rules to allow read access. This functionality mirrors previous rule updates.\n\nThe student side in `index.html` records submissions to `quizzes/{quizId}/submissions` upon completion, formatting results with fields such as student name, course section, score, violations, time spent, timestamp, and other existing fields.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Implementation plan to format student submissions to human-readable text and auto-load completed students in real-time in the teacher.html Submissions tab.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","Content":"\"# Implementation Plan: Human-Readable Auto-Submission & Live Submissions Feed\\n\\n## 1. Overview of Requested Changes\\n\\n1. **Student Submission Formatting in [index.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/index.html)**:\\n   - When a student completes the quiz under auto-submission mode (`settings.autoRecordQuiz !== false`), the submission payload posted to Firestore (`quizzes/{quizId}/submissions`) will include formatted, human-readable fields alongside the raw metrics:\\n     - `studentName`: Student's full name (e.g. `\\\"Juan Dela Cruz\\\"`).\\n     - `courseSection`: Student's course / section (